 "id": "V013",
 "title": "Play GTA 6 up to 18 hours early? Here's the catch",
 "audio": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3Lh3gaSoJDsjYAzqFyj65XamsxE/hf_20261117_053410_e1e73e8b-4898-44f9-8b71-f10efe77de4e.wav",
 "script": "You can play GTA 6 up to 18 hours early in the US. But there's a catch. New Zealand unlocks first, at midnight on November 19, which is 6 a.m. Eastern on the 18th. On Xbox, people set their console location to New Zealand. On PlayStation, you need a new New Zealand account and must pay in New Zealand dollars. Rockstar hasn't confirmed it works, and it may break Sony and Microsoft rules. Twitch reportedly warned one streamer about a ban. Risk it, or wait? Comment your pick.",
